\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Loved with everlasting love,
\par Led by grace that love to know;
\par Spirit, breathing from above,
\par Thou hast taught me it is so.
\par O this full and perfect peace!
\par O this transport all divine!
\par In a love which cannot cease
\par I am His, and He is mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Heaven above is softer blue,
\par Earth around is sweeter green;
\par Something lives in every hue,
\par Christless eyes have never seen:
\par Birds with gladder songs o'erflow,
\par Flowers with deeper beauties shine,
\par Since I know, as now I know,
\par I am His, and He is mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. His for ever, only His:
\par Who the Lord and me shall part?
\par Ah, with what a rest of bliss
\par Christ can fill the loving heart!
\par Heaven and earth may fade and flee,
\par First-born light in gloom decline;
\par But, while God and I shall be,
\par I am His, and He is mine.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
